Product Performance & Inventory Analysis — Manager Brief
Business problem
Optimize inventory levels and identify product opportunities to reduce stockouts and minimize overstock.

Executive summary
Analysis of five years of transaction data produced product-level KPIs and time-series exports to support replenishment, promotions, and SKU rationalization. Key outputs include Product_performance_file.csv and monthly_trend.csv for operational use.

Key insights
Top 20% of products generate ~80% of revenue (ABC Analysis) — focus inventory and promotions on these SKUs.
15 products flagged as high stockout risk (high coefficient of variation in monthly demand).
Seasonal patterns detected across 8 product categories — timing-sensitive stocking required.
12 products showing sustained declining sales (recent 3 months vs prior 3 months).
Clear fast/slow mover segmentation and wide variation in sales velocity across SKUs.
Business impact
Risk of lost sales for high-revenue fast movers if replenishment is not prioritized.
Working capital tied in slow-moving SKUs that should be considered for consolidation or liquidation.
Seasonal winners require advance procurement to capture peak demand.
Recommendations (actionable)
Prioritize replenishment and reduce lead time for Top 20% and fast-moving SKUs.
Implement safety-stock and shorter review cycles for the 15 high-risk SKUs.
Run a promotional pilot on the 12 declining products (test price/promote, monitor 4–8 weeks).
Liquidate or bundle slow-moving SKUs to free up working capital.
Build seasonal procurement calendar for the 8 seasonal categories (pre-stock before peaks).
Operationalize movement-based reorder rules (reorder points, review frequency, target days-of-supply).
Deliverables included
Product_performance_file.csv — product KPIs: revenue, quantity, first/last sale, days active, sales velocity, movement category, stockout risk, seasonality score, trend.
monthly_trend.csv — monthly time-series by product for forecasting and seasonality.
Suggested KPIs to monitor monthly
Coverage: % revenue from Top 20 SKUs
Stockout rate for Top 20 SKUs
SKUs with high CV (stockout risk)
% SKUs in decline (3-month trend)
Days-of-supply by movement category